WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.440
Spoofing may present differently from simple signal loss because the receiver can report a position or time that appears valid.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:17.123
Warning signs are therefore inconsistencies among the map, visual scene, compass, route, telemetry, and expected movement.

00:00:17.123 --> 00:00:34.027
Examples include an apparent jump while the aircraft is visibly stable, impossible speed or location, a map track that leaves the observed route, an unexpected home point, or navigation commands that do not fit the crew's view.

00:00:34.027 --> 00:00:45.223
Compass and G N S S disagreement may indicate several problems, including magnetic interference, calibration issues, sensor faults, reflected signals, or a navigation anomaly.

00:00:45.223 --> 00:00:50.711
Treat the mismatch as reduced confidence, not immediate proof of spoofing.

00:00:50.711 --> 00:00:53.565
Telemetry inconsistency matters over time.

00:00:53.565 --> 00:00:59.492
Compare commanded movement, groundspeed, direction, altitude source, visual references, and logged position.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:06.297
Preserve screenshots or notes only when doing so does not distract from safe control.

00:01:06.297 --> 00:01:11.346
Independent time or location references can strengthen review after landing.

00:01:11.346 --> 00:01:22.103
They should come from trusted systems with known provenance, not from another display that quietly depends on the same receiver or data source.

00:01:22.103 --> 00:01:26.713
Confirmation is difficult from one receiver and one symptom.

00:01:26.713 --> 00:01:35.714
High-confidence attribution may require specialized equipment, independent receivers, broader reports, technical expertise, and regulatory investigation outside the pilot's role.

00:01:35.714 --> 00:01:39.446
Operationally, distrust position-dependent automation when cues conflict.

00:01:39.446 --> 00:01:51.520
Simplify the mission, maintain visual control, use trained manual or degraded-mode procedures, move toward a safe landing area, and report the incident without overstating the cause.
